The attached image displays confocal microscopy images illustrating the uptake of AF647-labeled Nano-11 (red) and FITC-labeled ovalbumin (OVA, green) by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). The top row shows BMDCs incubated with Nano-11, indicating its internalization. The middle row with soluble OVA shows minimal uptake. The bottom row, representing Nano-11 with adsorbed OVA, demonstrates a significantly increased uptake of OVA and strong colocalization of both Nano-11 and OVA within the BMDCs (appearing yellow/orange). This indicates that Nano-11 effectively delivers negatively charged antigens to dendritic cells, a critical step for enhancing the immune response as an adjuvant.